{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788049924464308892,"compiled_state":{"alias":"hermitical-villainous-damselfly","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"9e616bf5ab40d81ba0bc395ff71178daeb41542000965a9c06881f30ae150ee1","event_uuid":"04ca4081-2efc-4ed5-a4e2-20d4c5f7a4f2","position":{"commit_sha":"4f058b5866a901c15df186d27c9d4650b6d1a13b","position":"1788046541848336939-04ca4081-2efc-4ed5-a4e2-20d4c5f7a4f2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788046541848336939,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context\n\nThe root tree holds 6,008 flat ticket directories and is 270 KB; every commit re-emits the WHOLE\nroot tree, so tree bytes are ~95% of the blobless pack. Sharding the flat namespace shrinks the\nper-commit root-tree object so each re-emission is far smaller — a durable structural reduction of\nthe tree churn that dominates the pack, complementing S1 (historical) and W1 (write-rate).\n\n## Scope\n\nShard the flat `tickets/<id>` layout into a fan-out namespace (e.g. `tickets/<quad-prefix>/<id>`)\nso a mutation re-emits only a small shard subtree plus a small top-level tree, not a 270 KB flat\nroot. Preserve ticket resolution (alias/short-id/full-id), event replay, and reconcile behavior.\nRequires a migration path for existing ticket paths.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThe history reclaim (S1) and the write-batching (W1). This is the on-disk tree LAYOUT.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Ticket storage uses a sharded fan-out layout; a single mutation re-emits only its shard subtree + a small top-level tree (measured tree bytes per commit drop substantially vs the 270 KB flat root).\n- [ ] Ticket resolution (alias, short-id, full-id) and event replay are unchanged (existing resolver/replay tests pass).\n- [ ] A migration maps existing flat paths to the sharded layout without losing or reassigning any ticket identity.\n- [ ] Reconcile/merge-as-union behavior is preserved on a reconvergence fixture.\n\n## Portability\n\nPure store-layout change with an in-process migration; no dependence on any single CI provider.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","536b-8930-b922-4063"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"a945-15b8-ff0e-4bfc","ticket_type":"task","title":"W2: shard the 6,008 flat ticket dirs to cut per-commit root-tree churn","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["04ca4081-2efc-4ed5-a4e2-20d4c5f7a4f2"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788049924464308892,"uuid":"77bb70fd-4bb8-4808-bbde-ff2ef54b9c1e"}